# Gemtext v1.1.0

I've released a small update to Gemtext{a}. At the moment, I'm working on adding Spartan protocol{b} support to Rogallo{c}, and to do this I need to handle a small extension it makes to Gemtext.

=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/ {a} Gemtext
=> https://portal.mozz.us/spartan/spartan.mozz.us/ {b} Spartan protocol
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/ {c} Rogallo

While Spartan is quite different from Gemini in the underlying protocol, it uses Gemtext as the default/standard markup language, but with one small difference. To allow uploaded data that is initiated by the markup, rather than by the server, there is a `=:` line type. In some respects, this is similar to type `7` items in Gopher maps.

Rather than spin up a whole new library just to support this one small difference, and rather than do some special-case nonsense in Rogallo itself, I've added optional (and turned on by default) support for `=:`. When encountered, this results in a `SpartanPrompt`{a} object, which simply inherits from a `Link`{b}.

=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/gemtext/#gemtext.SpartanPrompt {a} `SpartanPrompt`
=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/gemtext/#gemtext.Link {b} `Link`

Any code that doesn't require this feature can turn it off with the `with_spartan_support` parameter{a}.

=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/gemtext/#gemtext.Gemtext(with_spartan_support) {a} `with_spartan_support` parameter

